 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -19,7 +19,24 @@\n     features (they are standardized and a bias is added), so nonlinear structure only\n     helps if a feature expresses it. Only the Python standard library may be used.\n \n-    Current method: the raw inputs.\n+    Current method: engineered features.\n     \"\"\"\n-    return list(row)\n+    x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6 = row\n+    # 1. Magnitude squared of x1, x2\n+    f1 = x1**2 + x2**2\n+    # 2. Sign of interaction between x1, x2 (quadrant indicator)\n+    f2 = math.copysign(1, x1 * x2)\n+    # 3. Log transformation of skewed x3\n+    f3 = math.log(x3)\n+    # 4. Sum of absolute values of uniform variables x4, x5\n+    f4 = abs(x4) + abs(x5)\n+    # 5. Raw x6\n+    f5 = x6\n+    # 6. Interaction between normal x1 and skewed x3\n+    f6 = x1 * x3\n+    # 7. Sign of x1\n+    f7 = math.copysign(1, x1)\n+    # 8. Sign of x2\n+    f8 = math.copysign(1, x2)\n+    return [f1, f2, f3, f4, f5, f6, f7, f8]\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
